  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Galatians",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 5,
    "summary": "Stand fast in gospel liberty—Seek faith, love, Christ, and the Spirit—The works of the flesh and the fruits of the Spirit are named.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Stand fast therefore in the liberty wherewith Christ hath made us free, and be not entangled again with the yoke of bondage.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "Philip. 4:1 (1–7)."
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Liberty."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "2 Ne. 2:26 (26–27); Mosiah 5:8; Alma 61:9 (9, 21)."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "D&C 88:86."
          },
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 123,
            "text": "TG Bondage, Spiritual; Law of Moses."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, I Paul say unto you, that if ye be circumcised, Christ shall profit you nothing.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For I testify again to every man that is circumcised, that he is a debtor to do the whole law.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "Rom. 2:25."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Christ is become of no effect unto you, whosoever of you are justified by the law; ye are fallen from grace.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "TG Law of Moses."
          },
          {
            "start": 102,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "TG Grace."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For we through the Spirit wait for the hope of righteousness by faith.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "Rom. 5:2 (1–5); 1 Pet. 1:21 (21–22)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For in Jesus Christ neither circumcision availeth any thing, nor uncircumcision; but faith which worketh by love.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Circumcision."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "GR has any power, validity, service."
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 90,
            "text": "TG Faith."
          },
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 112,
            "text": "TG Love."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye did run well; who did hinder you that ye should not obey the truth?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "TG Disobedience."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "This persuasion cometh not of him that calleth you.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 22
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A little leaven leaveneth the whole lump.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I have confidence in you through the Lord, that ye will be none otherwise minded: but he that troubleth you shall bear his judgment, whosoever he be.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "TG Dependability."
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "GR will take no other view, will not have a different opinion."
          },
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "Gal. 1:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And I, brethren, if I yet preach circumcision, why do I yet suffer persecution? then is the offence of the cross ceased.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "GR stumbling block, cause of misery."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I would they were even cut off which trouble you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "TG Excommunication."
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "Gal. 1:8 (8–9)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For, brethren, ye have been called unto liberty; only use not liberty for an occasion to the flesh, but by love serve one another.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "TG Abundant Life; Liberty."
          },
          {
            "start": 112,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "TG Self-Sacrifice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 57
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For all the law is fulfilled in one word, even in this; Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Rom. 13:10 (8–10); 1 Tim. 1:5. TG God, Law of."
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "TG Love."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 46
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But if ye bite and devour one another, take heed that ye be not consumed one of another.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "This I say then, Walk in the Spirit, and ye shall not fulfil the lust of the flesh.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "TG Walking with God."
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Guidance, Divine."
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG Chastity; Lust."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the flesh lusteth against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh: and these are contrary the one to the other: so that ye cannot do the things that ye would.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Holy Ghost, Loss of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But if ye be led of the Spirit, ye are not under the law.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "D&C 20:45; 28:4; 42:13."
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "Acts 15:5 (1–11); Mosiah 13:29 (29–31)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Now the works of the flesh are manifest, which are these; Adultery, fornication, uncleanness, lasciviousness,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "Mosiah 16:3 (3–5); D&C 67:12 (10–12)."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG Fornication."
          },
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "TG Uncleanness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 57
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Idolatry, witchcraft, hatred, variance, emulations, wrath, strife, seditions, heresies,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "TG Strife."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Envyings, murders, drunkenness, revellings, and such like: of the which I tell you before, as I have also told you in time past, that they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Envy."
          },
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "TG Drunkenness; Word of Wisdom."
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Rioting and Reveling."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 114
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "Rom. 8:23. TG Holy Ghost, Mission of."
          },
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "TG Inspiration; Spirituality."
          },
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "Col. 3:12."
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Joy."
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "TG Contentment; Peace of God."
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "TG Forbear."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "TG Benevolence; Kindness."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "TG Faith."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Meekness, temperance: against such there is no law.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Meek."
          },
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "GR self-control. TG Temperance."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And they that are Christ’s have crucified the flesh with the affections and lusts.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "GR sufferings, afflictions, passions."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If we live in the Spirit, let us also walk in the Spirit.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let us not be desirous of vain glory, provoking one another, envying one another.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "TG Provoking."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "galatians6",
